From 0bb218f27c58b68549ef9d89ce56437f73b633f2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Minkovsky <dminkovsky@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 12:43:48 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Decide a failed move and its file from the move's pending
 record

The Storage Manager row read a failed move from release_storage.move_failed,
which followed coven_moves, and the changed file's name from coven_pending.
coven keeps the two in step, so a row with the flag and no file failed with
a disagreement no one could act on. coven_pending is now a table triggers can
follow, so release_storage keeps failed_move_file, the name of the file whose
original changed, from one read of the move's pending record. The listing's
move_failed and the row's Cancel follow it, the row reads the name from it,
and the status no longer fails on a failed move without a file.

